WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.674
Damping moves the state only a fraction toward its target.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.320
Here alpha is one half.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:11.200
Each update multiplies an error mode by one minus alpha mu.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.833
Alpha one: flips and grows.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:16.023
One half shrinks fast.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:17.799
One eighth shrinks slowly.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.510
Now many modes: each tick is one mode's mu.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:24.696
This line gives each mode's factor.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.570
Outside the band, seven modes grow.

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:31.017
A smaller alpha tilts the line toward flat.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:35.541
At two over mu max, the last mode reaches the edge.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.185
Smaller still, factors approach one.

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:41.638
The worst factor, rho, sets the rate.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:43.975
Alpha one diverges.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:46.307
One half: the error falls fast.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:50.295
One eighth crawls. Measured rates sit close to rho.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:54.290
Learned maps hide mu, so alpha stays small.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:59.996
It converges when every one minus alpha mu lies between minus one and one.
